[
  {
    "key": "pdd4.1.cumulativeAccuracy",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#41-measurement-views-fr-o1",
    "part": 0,
    "text": "The curve may be simplified for display. Simplification changes cumulative percentages by less than 0.2 percentage points. Statistics and percentile read-offs use all matching valid measurements.",
    "slots": []
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd4.3.unclassifiedLine",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#43-unclassified-records-d-12-proposed",
    "part": 0,
    "text": "Unclassified records excluded from scarp-type views: X (zero-slip initial stages).",
    "slots": ["X"]
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd5.2.shortDisclaimer",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#52-short-disclaimer",
    "part": 0,
    "text": "Research tool: simulated results, not site predictions. Interpret with professional judgment. [Full disclaimer →]",
    "slots": []
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd5.3.populationExplainer",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#53-population-explainer-fr-s6",
    "part": 0,
    "text": "**All model stages in the slip window** counts every recorded stage of every matching simulation inside your slip range — the measurements recorded at any stage within the range; with no slip window set, it counts every recorded stage. **One state per trial** counts only the last stage inside the window for each simulation — the measurements at the upper end of your range. With no slip window set, one state per trial is each simulation's final recorded state (approximately 5 m of slip). The two populations answer different questions and are never mixed.",
    "slots": []
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd5.4.scarpDipNotice",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#54-scarp-dip-provisional-notice-fr-o4-d-5",
    "part": 0,
    "text": "Provisional data: scarp-dip values await a correction from the research group; the largest errors are concentrated in the Simple scarp types. Treat scarp-dip results as provisional.",
    "slots": []
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd5.5.statisticsFraming",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#55-statistics-framing-cr-5",
    "part": 0,
    "text": "These are statistics of the matching simulation records. The median is a typical result among them; the 84th percentile is a commonly used higher fractile in deterministic engineering practice. No statistic here is a recommended design value — selecting a design value remains the responsibility of the engineer of record.",
    "slots": []
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd5.6.assistText",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#56-conversion-assist-fr-s5-d-3",
    "part": 0,
    "text": "You entered an anticipated vertical surface offset of {X} m. For each selected fault dip, this converts to the fault slip at depth shown here, using the ensemble's tested dip-specific relationship. The conversion assumes scarp height is approximately equal to vertical surface displacement — closest for Simple and Monoclinal scarps; Pressure Ridge scarps stand higher than the fault's vertical displacement, so the conversion tends to overstate slip where they dominate.",
    "slots": ["X"]
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd5.6.perDipLine",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#56-conversion-assist-fr-s5-d-3",
    "part": 1,
    "text": "{Dip}°: converted slip ≈ {Y} m — beyond the modeled range (approximately 0–5 m). Coverage for this dip is partial; matching simulations exist only up to the modeled maximum (≈5 m of slip).",
    "slots": ["Dip", "Y"]
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd5.6.rejectedEntryLine",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#56-conversion-assist-fr-s5-d-3",
    "part": 2,
    "text": "Enter the anticipated vertical surface offset (m) as a non-negative number — for example, 3 or 0.5. The value typed could not be read as one; the results still show the last valid scenario.",
    "slots": []
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd5.7.overlayFraming",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#57-field-overlay-framing-cr-6-fr-o5",
    "part": 0,
    "text": "Field measurements (black): **analogous, not identical.** Field and simulated values represent related but non-identical quantities; each field source is named with its own measure.",
    "slots": []
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd5.7.widthDefault",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#57-field-overlay-framing-cr-6-fr-o5",
    "part": 1,
    "text": "Width overlays default to measurements under the paper's 50 m criterion; larger field widths may include distributed, multi-strand deformation the model does not represent.",
    "slots": []
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd5.7.showAllWidths",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#57-field-overlay-framing-cr-6-fr-o5",
    "part": 2,
    "text": "[Show all field widths]",
    "slots": []
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd5.7.widthScopeNote",
    "source": "docs/app/pdd.md#57-field-overlay-framing-cr-6-fr-o5",
    "part": 3,
    "text": "Deformation-zone width measures the main modeled rupture zone. Real earthquakes can also produce separate deformation away from the main trace, which the model does not represent.",
    "slots": []
  },
  {
    "key": "pdd5.8.smallResultWarning",
